[#:seon.task{:name "an-attempts-cluster-facts-copy-onto-main-by-identity"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Phase AW1 of hybrid-agent-world.md (after AW0 and AW1a, `seon.db/entities-born-on-two-branches-of-one-commit-have-different-ids`: one eid counter per store, so a branch-born entity keeps its eid on main). The copy-back is git's squash merge over data (`merge --squash`: a three-way from the merge base, one commit on main, no parent link to the branch), never a cherry-pick and never datahike merge!/:parents. The pure `seon.merge/squash-merge` [source-db base-db target-db projection] -> {:tx-data :conflicts}: the branch's datoms since its merge base for `seon.program/cluster-attributes` (d/since on the branch; base = the immutable fork-point commit read with `datahike.api/commit-as-db` from `seon.cluster.registry/base-commit-id`; `seon.cluster.registry/fork!` creates its registry ref with `datahike.api/branch!`, and `seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch!` deletes both refs. At Datahike revision 61bca1edd6bcef079f5c47e4f5f75df30549934d, `datahike.gc/reachable-in-branch` seeds each registry head and marks its indexes regardless of remove-before; only parent traversal is time limited. No attribute history retention change), grouped by entity, replayed with eids unchanged (every eid was issued by this store; `seon.db/an-explicit-eid-outside-the-allocators-range-is-refused` guards the rest) except the collision remap: a new entity whose :db.unique/identity value (`seon.db/identity-attributes`, looked up on main's AVET) already exists on main takes main's eid in its own datoms and in every ref to it, because Datahike refuses an explicit eid carrying another entity's unique value (:transact/unique) instead of upserting it; classified per [e a] as `seon.program/three-way` classifies digests: unchanged -> nothing, only theirs -> assert or retract, only ours -> keep, both and different -> the entity schema's :seon.cluster/conflict rule: :theirs asserts, :ours keeps, :add is one :db.fn/call that sums (the occurrence count), :root keeps ours plus a conflict row {entity attribute base ours theirs}. It reuses the merge-request machinery instead of a second comparison: the base comes from `seon.cluster.source/merge-base` and `seon.cluster.source/branch-base-t` (made public), and `seon.program/changed-identities` and `seon.program/digest-map` take a projection argument (program attributes for merge requests, cluster attributes here) so both are one three-way with two projections. Proofs, a table on values with d/with targets: this test (main pulls the end, the refined intent and a child task by eid); a-value-changed-on-both-sides-resolves-by-the-declared-rule (table over :root, :theirs, :add; under :root the entity's other attribute still copies); program-and-runtime-facts-never-copy (a defn, an evaluation, a turn and a received message yield empty tx-data); a-copy-of-an-unchanged-branch-is-empty; a-retraction-on-the-branch-retracts-on-an-unchanged-main-only; a-branch-born-entity-keeps-its-eid-on-main (the child task's eid on main equals its eid on the branch, refs included; main's next allocation is unmoved); a-natural-identity-born-on-both-sides-maps-to-mains-eid (two branches each mint an occurrence with one signature: main holds one entity under its own eid, count summed by :add, every ref remapped); the-merge-base-is-the-merge-requests (the squash's base commit equals `seon.cluster.source/merge-base` for the same branch); the-merge-base-retains-the-count-needed-by-add (base occurrence count 1, source 2, unchanged target 1 yields 2); a-base-ref-keeps-the-fork-commit-only-until-retirement (cutoff after fork retains the commit while the work branch exists; retirement removes both refs and collection removes the commit); cost row: a ten-evaluation attempt under 10 ms / 5 MB through seon.profile/measure. Files: src/seon/cluster/squash.clj, test/seon/cluster/squash_test.clj, src/seon/cluster/source.clj (merge-base public), src/seon/program.cljc (projection argument)."
             :must-read #{seon.program/three-way seon.program/changed-identities seon.program/digest-map seon.program/program-attributes seon.program/cluster-attributes seon.cluster.source/merge-base seon.cluster.registry/fork! seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch! seon.cluster.registry/base-commit-id datahike.api/commit-as-db datahike.gc/gc-storage! seon.db/identity-attributes seon.db/with seon.profile/measure}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/hybrid-agent-world.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/eid-ranges-opus.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/eid-ranges-sol.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "disjoint-set-additions-merge-as-their-union"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(hybrid-done-and-merge M2) `seon.merge/squash-merge` merges cardinality-many attributes member by member, (ours - (base - theirs)) union (theirs - base), as git merges lines; `:seon.cluster/conflict` `:add` and `seon.merge/add-count` stay. Red proof: `seon.merge-test/disjoint-set-additions-merge-as-their-union` (base, ours adds y, theirs adds z on `:seon.task/evidence`: `:conflicts` is [] and main's value is base union {y} union {z}; today the two additions conflict). Cost: three-way on one changed task under 5 ms through `seon.profile/measure` (0.11-0.24 ms today). Files: `src/seon/cluster/squash.clj`, `test/seon/cluster/squash_test.clj`."
             :must-read #{seon.merge/squash-merge seon.merge/add-count seon.program/three-way seon.profile/measure}
             :needs #{[:seon.task/sym seon.context/a-proof-green-before-the-work-is-not-done]}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-done-and-merge.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-conflict-keeps-its-three-values-on-the-merge-branch"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(hybrid-done-and-merge M4) A both-sides-changed coordinate with no declared `:seon.cluster/conflict` rule becomes a `:seon.merge/unmerged` entity on the merge branch only (new schema `resources/seon/schemas/seon.merge.edn`; `seon.id/id [assignment attribute entity-identity]`; members `attribute`, `entity`, `base`, `ours`, `theirs`, `source-commit`; any write to the coordinate on the merge branch retracts it). Delete `seon.merge/conflict-task!`; convert `db_flow_test` (680) and `squash_test` (101). Red proof: `seon.merge-test/a-conflict-keeps-its-three-values-on-the-merge-branch` (pulled base, ours, theirs and source-commit equal the values merged). Cost: under 50 ms. Platform slice (`--test`)."
             :must-read #{seon.merge/conflict-task! seon.merge/squash-merge seon.program/three-way seon.id/id}
                         :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-done-and-merge.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-merge-whose-reached-definition-moved-writes-nothing"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(hybrid-done-and-merge M7) The gate is the one rule; designed reds are data. `seon.context/step-status` on the merge branch at main's head B replaces `seon.cluster.source/accept-merge!`'s red-test refusal and `seon.test/change-reds`; coverage accepts a designed red (`seon.context/designed-red?` made public: a failure of type `:seon.error/unimplemented` on a deftest whose `:seon/tasks` names a task with no `:merged` assignment); `merge-tx`'s compare-and-swap of the tested digests replaces `seon.cluster.source/declarations-held-tx`; `:parents` dropped. Delete `seon.test/change-reds` and its `test_test` cases (362-386). Red proofs: `seon.cluster.merge-test/a-merge-whose-reached-definition-moved-writes-nothing` (tx-data [], `:seon.task/outcome` absent), `a-prove-steps-designed-reds-pass-the-gate` (an `:seon.error/unimplemented` red tagged to an open task: :merged; the same red with an untyped error: the coordinate stays unmerged on the merge branch). Cost: gate reuse on an unchanged result under 100 ms. After M6."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/accept-merge! seon.cluster.source/declarations-held-tx seon.test/change-reds seon.context/designed-red? seon.context/step-status}
             :needs #{[:seon.task/sym seon.context/every-agent-sees-where-its-reds-came-from]}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-done-and-merge.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-accepted-merge-is-published-by-the-next-pass"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(hybrid-done-and-merge M9, narrowed by plan.md §0 item 1) Publication is derived due work, not a step of the merge: `seon.merge/merge!` stops writing back; `seon.cluster.agent/next-actions` derives `:publish` from `seon.cluster.agent/lifecycle-facts`' `:seon.flow.plan/publish?` (an assignment `:merged` with `:seon.task/merge-commit`, its merge request on main, no `:seon.task/git-commit` and no `:seon.task/refusal`), and `:delete-branch` waits for it. `seon.merge/publish!` derives the accepted merge from main (`seon.cluster.source/merge-accepted`), writes into the checkout `seon.merge/checkout` resolves from `:seon.config.fs/working-root` (`seon.cluster.source/write-back!`) and commits exactly those paths (`seon.cluster.source/commit!`) under the claim `merge-<assignment>` in `bin/lane`'s ledger; a path another lane claims or leaves dirty waits (`seon.cluster.source/waiting-paths`); a refusal is recorded as `:seon.task/refusal`, never as an `:error` end over `:merged`. A crash anywhere leaves it due. Red proof: `seon.cluster.merge-test/an-accepted-merge-is-published-by-the-next-pass` (after `my.root/merge!` `:merge-commit` present, `:git-commit` absent and no file written; a lane's claim makes the pass wait; the next pass writes `:git-commit` equal to the checkout's HEAD; a second pass changes nothing). Cost: under 1 s for the small file case."
             :must-read #{seon.merge/merge! seon.merge/publish! seon.merge/checkout seon.cluster.agent/next-actions seon.cluster.agent/lifecycle-facts seon.cluster.source/write-back! seon.cluster.source/commit! seon.cluster.source/merge-accepted seon.cluster.source/waiting-paths}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-done-and-merge.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/prebrief-m9-m8a.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-sibling-merge-that-breaks-a-proof-undoes-done"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(hybrid-done-and-merge M11) New `seon.merge/update!` merges main into the source branch when the source is done and the gate on the merge result is not (a sibling's merge turned a reached test red): the same three-way with source = main and target = the agent's branch, `:seon.task/merge-base` moved to main's commit M by `seon.merge/update-tx`, unmerged coordinates written to the agent's branch as `:seon.merge/unmerged` for the agent; the agent's next eval request reruns the proofs pending at the new reach digests. Red proof: `seon.cluster.merge-test/a-sibling-merge-that-breaks-a-proof-undoes-done` (the source answers :working after the update and :done after the proof's rerun). Cost: update! under 50 ms. After M7; `src/seon/turn.clj` as a patch."
             :must-read #{seon.merge/squash-merge seon.context/step-status seon.turn/prove-turn seon.cluster.source/accept-merge!}
             :needs #{[:seon.task/sym seon.merge/a-merge-whose-reached-definition-moved-writes-nothing]}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-done-and-merge.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "main-keeps-the-merge-results-after-the-branch-is-deleted"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(hybrid-test-results R8, after M7) Root reads branches and the merge gate's answers stay on main. Root's `seon.test.runner/results-at` databases are main and every live branch head; the gate's run on the merge branch is admitted on main through R5's `seon.test/admit-run` (tested branch the merge branch), as root recording its own observation (owner: decided). Red proof: new `seon.cluster.merge-test/main-keeps-the-merge-results-after-the-branch-is-deleted`: after merge and branch deletion, `results-at` on main holds the gate's results at the merged keys and root's next request executes no body for them (HEAD: `:seon.data` runs stay on the deleted branch). Cost: recording increment under 100 ms; root's read over live branch heads under 20 ms (0.15 ms per head). Files: `src/seon/test/runner.clj`, `src/seon/test.clj`, M7's merge owner (today `seon.cluster.source/accept-merge!`), `test/seon/cluster/merge_test.clj`"
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/accept-merge! seon.test/admit-run seon.test.runner/result-at-reach seon.context/main-database}
             :needs #{[:seon.task/sym seon.merge/a-merge-whose-reached-definition-moved-writes-nothing] [:seon.task/sym seon.test/a-base-run-is-kept-on-the-agents-branch]}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-test-results.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-jvms-first-facts-merge-follows-the-changed-facts"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(m6-notes.md, measured with `seon.profile/measure` in a check JVM) A facts merge through `my.root/merge!` costs 6.4 ms and 1 MB warm, but as a fresh JVM's first merge 417 ms and 1.0 GB, 359 ms of it in `seon.db/vector-query-call` (the first three-way and projection reads in `seon.merge/merge!`). The work must follow the changed facts, not the first call: find which first-call derivation (projection read, squash three-way) allocates the gigabyte, and derive it from what the merge reads. Red proof: `my.root-test/a-jvms-first-facts-merge-follows-the-changed-facts` asserts under 100 ms and 64 MB on the thread, red only when it is its JVM's first merge (run alone through `bin/seon check`). Done when it is green alone."
             :must-read #{seon.merge/merge! my.root/merge! seon.db/vector-query-call}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/m6-notes.md"}}]
